==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Your first encounter (in theory) with Dread Bore!

Deploy a small group of cats that can withstand the first waves of peons, initiate the boss, and force Dread Bore to dig. Once Dread Bore unburrows, deploy as many Zombie Killers as possible ([[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Gardener Cat]], [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Welterweight Cat]], and [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Vaulter Cat]] are your best options since they can control Dread Bore reliably). The Aliens shouldn't be much of a threat here, unless you lack [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]].

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The only thing that changes here is that The Thrillerz replaces the other peons, so you can use the strategy from the previous chapter here.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This outbreak version of The Great Abyss is drastically different from the previous two. To defeat this stage, the [[Anti-unstarred Alien Treasures]] are almost necessary. [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], as well as attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] will be your best options for handling these sheer numbers. You win when you kill Bun Bun Symbiote.

